    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>70</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math> meters",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> meters",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> be the centres of the two circles where the poles of height <math><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and <math><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> respectively stand making angles <math><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mn>6</mn><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> respectively at the point <math><mi>O</mi></math> where these circles touch each other externally.<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0017_fa04d28b22bf.png\" style=\"width:2.24653in;height:1.72014in\" /><br />The sum of the radii of the two circles = The distance between the centres of the two circles.<br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cot</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cot</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;meters"
  }
